OL,3,GNEWSARare glimpse inside theatre closed
OL,4,Asince 1998
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe first thing visitors notice is the
OL,7,Fdoor.
OL,9,FAfter 28 years shut, it creaks open to
OL,10,Freveal a dark corridor where, as I
OL,11,Fjoined the rare few taking a step
OL,12,Finside, paint peels from walls and bare
OL,13,Flight bulbs hang from the ceiling.
OL,15,FBut beyond the signs of decay lies a
OL,16,Fsurprise: an ornate auditorium that has
OL,17,Fsurvived decades of neglect and is now
OL,18,Fat the centre of ambitious plans to
OL,19,Fbring one of a city's most treasured
OL,20,Ftheatres back to life.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,359,350,200,160,0,100
